dict(id='B1',statement='On a finite union of independent complete rational affine d-planes through a rational common origin, a continuous function is printed-PC exactly when every branch restriction is ordinary convex and all origin values agree.',proof='Translate the rational origin to zero and identify saturated branch lattices. Independence means the sum of the branch linear spaces is direct; it does not mean only pairwise zero intersections. Necessity of branch convexity follows by the complete local rational-midpoint argument R1 in the whole joint proof below, using the inherited rational branch complex: every such local branch PCC is also a PCC of X, and continuity gives ordinary local convexity and then segment convexity on the complete branch. This uses refinement and incidence, not coarsening. Origin agreement follows from continuity/single-valuedness. Conversely let each branch function be convex with the same value a at zero. For a printed legal PCC centered at x!=0, its center face contains a nonzero point on a unique branch. Every incident endpoint cell therefore lies on that branch, so convexity applies. At x=0 group endpoints by branch (zero endpoints may be assigned anywhere), and put A_i=sum of the group weights. Direct-sum independence of the barycentric zero equation gives sum_{j in i} alpha_j x_j=0 in EACH branch. For A_i>0, ordinary convexity gives sum_{j in i} alpha_j f_i(x_j)>=A_i a. Sum the finite inequalities; discard zero coefficients and empty groups. Thus the origin PCC is valid. Cells of an arbitrary refinement remain contained in individual branches, since a connected positive-dimensional convex cell cannot leave one branch through its sole intersection point without including a segment outside X. A lower-dimensional origin cell is common; all other cells are unique. This proves sufficiency for every printed rational refinement and all actual real relation weights.'),
dict(id='B2',statement='Every continuous PC function boundedly relative to an actual REAL positive-growth reference on this independent-branch union has GLOBAL decreasing real-PA regularization on rational geometry with the SAME reference.',proof='Apply the entire independently reconstructed full-affine actual-REAL-reference regularization proof E1,R1,R2,R3 in the joint proof below separately to f_i on each saturated complete branch, with actual reference gamma_i. This is a working proof dependency included in full, not an accepted sixth grant. It supplies actual finite rational-geometry real PA convex q_{i,n} with global error at most eta_n/2, eta_n=2^-n. Let a=f(0), a single real number. Define theta_{i,n}=q_{i,n}-q_{i,n}(0)+a. Its error from f_i is at most eta_n everywhere, and its origin value is EXACTLY a on EVERY branch. No rational approximation of a is required in PA_R. Refine the finite rational carrying complexes to contain the rational origin as a face; affine formulas are unchanged and no irrational wall is introduced. Since there are finitely many independent branches, their union is a finite rational common complex. The theta_{i,n} glue to a continuous real PA function theta_n; B1 gives PC. It is boundedly relative to the ACTUAL gamma with global error at most eta_n from f. Define F_n=theta_n+4eta_n. Then 3eta_n<=F_n-f<=5eta_n globally. As eta_{n+1}=eta_n/2, F_{n+1}-f<=2.5eta_n<3eta_n<=F_n-f, so F_n decreases everywhere (strictly by at least eta_n/2) to f uniformly on ALL X. These are genuine actual-reference PA_R PC approximants on rational spatial geometry. This is not a change of recession, an irrational max construction, a literal PA_Z approximation or a local-only completion. Constant shifts do not change branch growth. Arbitrary positive REAL constant branch weights affect only the raw cycle, not this construction.'),
